// The message manifest (B3 of 0.7.15, BUG-1136; docs/04-netcode.md#netcode-manifest): every top-level message type
// of the protocol, listed exactly once, and the message families with their wire revisions (B6, BUG-1137). An
// X-macro file: the includer defines MSG and / or FAMILY, this file #undefs them at the end.
//
// Generated from it (never kept by hand):
//   * `enum net::MsgType` (net/protocol.h): a duplicate name does not compile, a duplicate id fails the switches below
//   * the direction of each type and the host's direction gate (net/manifest.h msg_dir, dir_gate_drops)
//   * the world-state class (host_world.h msg_class, BUG-0420) and the dispatch route of the session's custom-message
//     callback (net/manifest.h dispatch_route, session_glue.cpp)
//   * the message table of docs/04-netcode.md (tools/msg_manifest.py docs; `make test` checks it)
//   * the family revisions a HELLO / WELCOME carries (CAP_FAMILIES) and the hash lock of each family's wire
//     (net/messages.lock, tools/msg_manifest.py check in `make test`)
//
// MSG(id, NAME, chan, dir, cls, route, recv, family, "what")
//   chan    R reliable, U unreliable, RU both (docs only)
//   dir     who sends it on the wire: Host (host -> guests), Guest (guest -> host; the host may relay it), Any
//   cls     host_world::MsgClass: Session (wherever the guest plays), HostWorld (a guest elsewhere drops it at
//           dispatch), Module (the module gates it per place)
//   recv    which game's session_glue dispatch takes it: Both, Host, Client (the other role ignores it there)
//   route   the handler of session_glue.cpp's dispatch (net::Route); None: net::Session handles it or nobody does
//   family  the message family (FAMILY below) whose revision covers its wire format
//
// FAMILY(name, id, rev, minor, stages, "title", "wire files")
//   rev     bumped when older versions can NOT read the family's messages any more (a changed field, a removed type):
//           a peer with another rev of a family the current stage uses is refused (net/compat.h)
//   minor   bumped for a change older versions still read (a new trailing field, a new type they ignore): a warning only
//   stages  where the family is used: STAGE_ALWAYS, or STAGE_CELL | STAGE_CREATURE | STAGE_TRIBE | STAGE_CIV | STAGE_SPACE
//           (an adventure counts as Creature)
//   wire files: sources (under mods/coop/) whose code, without comments, is part of the family's lock hash
// Every 0.7.x before 0.7.15 sends no revisions: it counts as rev 1 minor 0 of every family listed here (compat.h).
// A changed row or wire file without a bumped rev / minor fails `make test` (tools/msg_manifest.py check); then bump
// and run `tools/msg_manifest.py lock`.

#ifndef MSG
#define MSG(id, name, chan, dir, cls, route, recv, family, what)
#endif
#ifndef FAMILY
#define FAMILY(name, id, rev, minor, stages, title, files)
#endif

// Minor bumps of fix/w53-cellvote: cell 1.1 (MSG_CELL_FOOD's own-editor spend, MSG_CELL_MATE: BUG-1249, BUG-1246),
// npc 1.1 (wsync row cell_spend_ack, BUG-1249), creature 1.1 (no wire change: the guest opens its own landfall editor
// after a late arrival, BUG-1240; a host does not wait for such a guest's arrival, vote.cpp core.arrival_nowait).
// Minor bumps of feat/w56-dna (WP-D, BUG-1291, own DNA per player): creature 1.2 (MSG_DNA's tail: flags, the party bar,
// the world; the total is the guest's own DNA), npc 1.2 (wsync row cell_spent_own). A peer below these plays the shared
// pool with the host (dna_own.h peer_reads).
// Minor bump of feat/w54-line: creations 1.1 (MSG_SPECIES_LINE, the species line of WP-0, BUG-1270; older peers drop the
// type at dispatch).
// feat/w54-shims: creations stays 1.1 (unreleased): WP-C2's MSG_CREATION kind 9 (a player's own design) is gone, the
// designs go as line creations of MSG_SPECIES_LINE (species::set_design); a kind 9 is dropped as any unknown kind.
// fix/w56-sync: no npc bump of its own (0.7.15.2 ships npc 1.1, 0.7.16 npc 1.2 with feat/w56-dna): MSG_NPC_STATE /
// SPAWN flag NF_ALPHA 64 (BUG-1283) and MSG_PLAYER_RULE kind K_DRAMA 11 (BUG-1282), both ignored by older peers; a guest
// uses them only from a host with npc 1.2 or newer (net/compat.h kNpcMinorWorldEvents).
// Minor bump of fix/w56-sync: civ 1.1 (MSG_CIV_STATE chunk 0xF9 kInfluenceChunk, chunks 0: the cities' follower maps,
// converters, buy meters and price maps, BUG-1285 / BUG-1287; an older guest drops it as a bad snapshot header).
// Minor bump of fix/w59-tribe: session 1.2 (MSG_DIAG's digest: a trailing u8 `stands`, the sender's game time stands,
// BUG-1339; an older reader stops before it, an older sender's digest reads 0: compared as before).
// WP-0 of 0.7.17 (docs/plan-0.7.17.md "WP-0"): the minors of 0.7.17, bumped once before the work packages start so
// that parallel branches do not each bump the same family (one bump per family per release). Only minors: a 0.7.16.1
// peer (session 1.2, world 1.0, creature 1.2, cell 1.1, civ 1.1, space 1.2, creations 1.1) still joins and every
// existing message reads as before (net/compat.h refuses only another rev; every gate on a minor is "this minor or
// newer"). A new path of a WP is gated on its family's new minor (`peer_families` on the host, `host_families` on a
// guest, BUG-1282): civ 1.2 (WP-M1 own Civ money, MSG 74), session 1.3 (WP-H1 own stage history, MSG 75), creature 1.3
// (WP-P2 own progress in Creature, MSG 76; WP-R1 revive, MSG 77), cell 1.2 (WP-P1 own progress in Cell), space 1.3
// (WP-S1 fleets, MSG 78), creations 1.2 (WP-K1 captain, WP-L2 lineage cells: MSG_CREATION kinds 10-12), world 1.1
// (WP-W1 the share's file list). Until 0.7.17 ships these minors are open: a WP that changes a family's rows or wire
// files re-locks it without another bump, `tools/msg_manifest.py lock --rebase <family> "<WP>: <what>, unreleased
// <family> 1.x of 0.7.17"` (as feat/w54-shims did for creations 1.1 in 0.7.16). The ids 74-78 and the kinds 10-12 are
// reserved in net/manifest.h kReservedMsgs and creations.h.
// WP-S1 of 0.7.17 (fix/w73-fleet, BUG-1288): space 1.3 adds MSG_UFO_LEAD 78 and wire/space_ufo.h (the NPC ships of a
// place without the host, led by a guest the host names; a peer before space 1.3 is never sent it nor named).
// 0.7.17.1 (BUG-1539): space 1.4 appends optional trailing u32 mission_id to wire::space_core::Mission (K_MISSION);
// older readers stop before it, and newer readers accept old K_MISSION payloads with mission_id = 0.
// WP-0 of 0.7.99 (docs/plan-0.7.99.md): pre-0.8 release minors bumped once so parallel WPs never collide:
// creature 1.4 (WP-A co-op Galactic Adventures MSG 79 ADVENTURE, BUG-1474/0793; WP-G guest pack recruit BUG-1256;
// WP-F post-editor nest proxies BUG-1388), cell 1.3 (WP-G Cell friendly fire BUG-0899; WP-F rescale centre BUG-1394),
// tribe 1.2 (WP-G Tribe friendly fire BUG-0899; WP-F chief hold/facing BUG-1347/1458), civ 1.3 (WP-G Civ friendly fire
// BUG-0899, citizen gestures BUG-1231; WP-F city decorations BUG-1456, vehicle burst BUG-0438), space 1.5 (WP-F colony
// citizen lead BUG-1404), creations 1.3 (WP-Q shared creations library BUG-0873).
// WP-0 of 0.8.0 (docs/plan-0.8.md): Rivals + 0.8.0 release minors bumped once so parallel WPs never collide:
// session 1.4 (WP-R1 MSG 80 RIVALS, BUG-0794; WP-Q CAP_JOIN_PROOF password, BUG-0867; WP-C CAP_RESUME_WORLD, BUG-0869),
// world 1.2 (WP-C Cell warm reconnect receipt, BUG-0869), creature 1.5 (WP-AE MSG 82 ADV_EDITOR, BUG-0863; WP-R3 Creature
// Rivals, BUG-1547), npc 1.3 (WP-R3..R6 MSG 81 RIVALS_FACTION; WP-T Tribe UFO mirror, BUG-1543), cell 1.4 (WP-R2 Cell
// Rivals, BUG-1546), tribe 1.3 (WP-R4 Tribe Rivals, BUG-1548; WP-T epic fix, BUG-1542), civ 1.4 (WP-R5 Civ Rivals,
// BUG-1549), space 1.6 (WP-R6 Space Rivals, BUG-1550).
FAMILY(session,   1, 1, 4, STAGE_ALWAYS, "session", "net/protocol.h wire/history.h wire/rivals.h")
FAMILY(world,     2, 1, 2, STAGE_ALWAYS, "world transfer", "world_resume.h")
FAMILY(creature,  3, 1, 5, STAGE_CREATURE, "Creature", "wire/adventure.h")
FAMILY(npc,       4, 1, 3, STAGE_CREATURE | STAGE_TRIBE | STAGE_CIV, "mirrored creature and world state", "wire/rivals_faction.h")
FAMILY(cell,      5, 1, 4, STAGE_CELL, "Cell", "")
FAMILY(tribe,     6, 1, 3, STAGE_TRIBE, "Tribe", "wire/tribe_anim.h")
FAMILY(civ,       7, 1, 4, STAGE_CIV | STAGE_SPACE, "Civilization", "")
FAMILY(space,     8, 1, 6, STAGE_SPACE, "Space", "wire/common.h wire/space_core.h wire/space_map.h wire/space_contracts.h wire/space_diplomacy.h wire/space_finale.h wire/space_rivalry.h wire/space_allies.h wire/space_trade.h wire/space_planets.h wire/space_badges.h wire/space_eco.h wire/space_ufo.h")
FAMILY(shared,    9, 1, 0, STAGE_TRIBE | STAGE_CIV | STAGE_SPACE, "shared resources", "wire/common.h wire/shared_res.h")
FAMILY(creations, 10, 1, 3, STAGE_ALWAYS, "creations", "species_line_core.h library_core.h")

// Class notes (from the 0.7.14 switch of host_world.h): ANIM, DAMAGE are Session: a partner's own creature (its
// puppet); SETTINGS, COLORS, REPORT, HOST_WORLD: the session's, wherever the guest plays (HOST_WORLD is what
// "elsewhere" is measured against); VOTE: session-wide, the editor start it brings is gated in its handler
// (core.vote_world); RES: held inside shared.cpp (res.elsewhere), not at dispatch.
// Ids 55 and 58 are free (never used). Ids 74-78 are reserved for 0.7.17 (net/manifest.h kReservedMsgs: 74 CIV_WALLET,
// 75 PLAYER_HISTORY, 76 PROGRESS, 77 RESCUE, 78 UFO_LEAD); any other new type takes the next free id after 78.
MSG(1,  HELLO,       R,  Guest, Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "u16 protocol, u32 exe build id, str8 name; then u32 caps and their payloads (#netcode-hello-caps)")
MSG(2,  WELCOME,      R,  Host,  Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "u8 your id, u32 world id, u8 n, n x {u8 id, str8 name}; then u32 caps and their payloads")
MSG(3,  REJECT,       R,  Host,  Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "u8 reason (1 version, 2 full, 3 another exe build, 4 started, 5 kicked), str8 text")
MSG(4,  PLAYER_JOIN,  R,  Host,  Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "u8 id, str8 name, str8 version")
MSG(5,  PLAYER_LEAVE, R,  Host,  Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "u8 id, u8 reason")
MSG(6,  PLAYER_STATE, U,  Any,   Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "a player's own creature: pose, flags, health, species, mode, world, scale, agl, body (the host relays it)")
MSG(7,  CHAT,         R,  Any,   Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "u8 id, str16 text (the host relays it)")
MSG(8,  PING,         U,  Guest, Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "unused: nothing sends it, the host answers one with a PONG")
MSG(9,  PONG,         U,  Host,  Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "unused: the answer to PING")
MSG(10, BYE,          U,  Any,   Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "leaving (three packets)")
MSG(11, ABILITY,      R,  Any,   Session,   None,        Both,   session,   "reserved, never sent or handled")
MSG(12, DAMAGE,       R,  Any,   Session,   Npc,         Both,   npc,       "host -> guest: an NPC hit you; guest -> host: friendly fire on a player (F3)")
MSG(13, NPC_STATE,    U,  Host,  Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "u32 time, u8 n, n x NpcState (+ agl trailer)")
MSG(14, WORLD_OFFER,  R,  Host,  Session,   World,       Client, world,     "the host's save follows: u32 world, u32 size, u16 files, str8 planet")
MSG(15, WORLD_FILE,   R,  Host,  Session,   World,       Client, world,     "a file header: u16 index, u32 size, str8 path")
MSG(16, WORLD_CHUNK,  R,  Host,  Session,   World,       Client, world,     "file data: u16 index, u32 offset, u16 n, bytes")
MSG(17, WORLD_DONE,   R,  Host,  Session,   World,       Client, world,     "end of the transfer: u32 world id; optional trailing u64 resume_receipt, u8 flags (bit 0: warm reconnect accepted, world_resume.h, BUG-0869)")
MSG(18, ANIM,         R,  Any,   Session,   Anim,        Both,   creature,  "an animation of a player's own creature (the host relays it)")
MSG(19, NPC_SPAWN,    R,  Host,  Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "start mirroring an NPC (NpcSpawn)")
MSG(20, NPC_DESPAWN,  R,  Host,  Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "stop mirroring an NPC: u16 id")
MSG(21, DAMAGE_REQ,   R,  Guest, Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "my hit on an NPC: u16 id, f32 damage, i32 type")
MSG(22, WORLD_TIME,   U,  Host,  HostWorld, WorldTime,   Client, creature,  "the time of day: the sky's quaternion")
MSG(23, DNA,          R,  Host,  HostWorld, Dna,         Client, creature,  "the DNA total (f32: the shared pool, or this guest's own DNA), u8 n x {cause, player, f32} (dna_ledger.h), u8 pace, u8 flags + f32 party bar + u32 world (dna_own.h)")
MSG(24, DNA_ADD,      R,  Guest, Session,   DnaAdd,      Host,   creature,  "DNA a guest earned or spent (f32 delta)")
MSG(25, RES,          R,  Host,  Session,   Shared,      Both,   shared,    "a shared resource total (u8 id, f64)")
MSG(26, RES_ADD,      R,  Guest, Session,   Shared,      Both,   shared,    "a guest's change of a shared resource (u8 id, f64 delta)")
MSG(27, PING_MARK,    R,  Any,   Session,   PingMark,    Both,   session,   "a look-here marker: u8 origin, vec3, u32 mode (the host relays it)")
MSG(28, READY,        R,  Guest, Session,   Ready,       Host,   session,   "u8 ready")
MSG(29, LOBBY,        R,  Host,  Session,   Lobby,       Client, session,   "u8 n, {u8 id, u8 ready, u16 rtt}, roles (lobby.h)")
MSG(30, NOTICE,       R,  Any,   Session,   Notice,      Both,   session,   "str8 text everybody sees (the host relays it)")
MSG(31, TRIBE_STATE,  U,  Host,  HostWorld, Tribe,       Both,   tribe,     "tribes and citizens snapshot (chunked)")
MSG(32, TRIBE_CMD,    R,  Guest, HostWorld, Tribe,       Both,   tribe,     "an order for the guest's own tribe members")
MSG(33, CELL_STATE,   U,  Host,  HostWorld, Cell,        Both,   cell,      "NPC cells and food snapshot (chunked)")
MSG(34, CELL_HIT,     R,  Any,   HostWorld, Cell,        Both,   cell,      "guest -> host: u32 host cell index, u8 damage, u8 type (host -> guest only from the test command coop.pool hurt)")
MSG(35, CELL_EAT,     R,  Guest, HostWorld, Cell,        Both,   cell,      "u32 host cell index the guest ate or destroyed")
MSG(36, CELL_FOOD,    R,  Any,   HostWorld, Cell,        Both,   cell,      "host: i32 food, i32 plant; guest: i32 delta, u8 plant, u32 meal, i32 own cell editor spend (BUG-1249)")
MSG(37, CIV_STATE,    U,  Host,  HostWorld, Civ,         Both,   civ,       "cities and vehicles snapshot (chunked)")
MSG(38, CIV_CMD,      R,  Any,   Module,    Civ,         Both,   civ,       "guest -> host: a vehicle order, move, purchase or building; host -> guest: a specialty ask, a Space planner building")
MSG(39, CIV_BUILD,    R,  Host,  HostWorld, Civ,         Both,   civ,       "a building appeared in a city, a city founded, the trade routes")
MSG(40, UFO_STATE,    U,  Host,  Module,    Squadron,    Both,   space,     "NPC ships near the guest (chunked)")
MSG(41, UFO_HIT,      R,  Guest, Module,    Squadron,    Both,   space,     "u16 ship id, f32 damage, i32 type, vec3 dir")
MSG(42, UFO_DAMAGE,   R,  Host,  Module,    Squadron,    Both,   space,     "f32 damage, i32 type, vec3 dir, u16 attacker ship id")
MSG(43, VOTE,         R,  Host,  Session,   Vote,        Client, creature,  "the evolution vote: u8 active, u8 seconds, str8 text, u32 editor, u8 flags")
MSG(44, CELL_KO,      R,  Any,   HostWorld, Cell,        Both,   cell,      "u8 player, u8 state, u8 tenths left, u8 revive progress (the host relays it)")
MSG(45, CREATION,     R,  Any,   Session,   Creation,    Both,   creations, "reliable chunks of a player's creation")
MSG(46, ROLE,         R,  Guest, Session,   Role,        Host,   civ,       "u8 role (Civilization: none, military, economic, religious)")
MSG(47, CIV_ALARM,    R,  Host,  HostWorld, Civ,         Both,   civ,       "u8 city index, u8 kind, u8 owner")
MSG(48, SPACE,        R,  Any,   Module,    Space,       Both,   space,     "u8 kind (space_kinds.def), u8 origin, payload (the host relays it)")
MSG(49, CELL_BITTEN,  R,  Guest, HostWorld, Cell,        Both,   cell,      "u32 host cell index of the NPC whose mirror bit the guest")
MSG(50, SPECIES,      R,  Host,  HostWorld, Social,      Both,   creature,  "the Creature stage's species relationship table")
MSG(51, SOCIAL,       R,  Any,   HostWorld, Social,      Both,   creature,  "u8 kind: a social act, its progress, its result, a goal reward")
MSG(52, NEST,         RU, Any,   HostWorld, Nest,        Both,   creature,  "u8 kind: the eggs at the host's nests, an egg a guest ate")
MSG(53, PARTS,        R,  Any,   HostWorld, Parts,       Both,   creature,  "the party's collected creature parts")
MSG(54, WOBJ,         RU, Any,   Module,    Wobj,        Both,   npc,       "u8 kind: host-owned world objects (snapshot), a guest's request")
MSG(56, FIELDS,       U,  Host,  HostWorld, Fields,      Both,   npc,       "replicated state fields of mirrored objects (fields.h)")
MSG(57, NPC_RESYNC,   R,  Guest, Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "u8 n, n x u16 NPC ids the guest has states and no spawn of")
MSG(59, NPC_ANIM,     RU, Host,  Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "animations the host's NPCs and tribe members started or play now")
MSG(60, DIAG,         RU, Any,   Session,   Diag,        Both,   session,   "support diagnostics (net/diagmsg.h): u8 kind, payload")
MSG(61, EFFECT,       R,  Any,   Module,    Effect,      Both,   creature,  "a player's creature started or stopped an effect (the host relays it)")
MSG(62, WSTATE,       U,  Host,  HostWorld, Wsync,       Both,   npc,       "host-owned world state rows (wsync.h)")
MSG(63, PLAYER_RULE,  RU, Any,   HostWorld, PlayerRule,  Both,   npc,       "u8 kind: the game's rules one game decides on the other's creature (a stun)")
MSG(64, MIRROR_FX,    RU, Host,  HostWorld, MirrorFx,    Both,   npc,       "what the host's game did to a mirrored creature (effect, voice, sprint)")
MSG(65, NPC_MEAT,     RU, Any,   Module,    Npc,         Both,   npc,       "u8 kind: the meat left on killed NPCs, what a guest ate of it")
MSG(66, SETTINGS,     R,  Host,  Session,   Settings,    Both,   session,   "the session settings (settings_core.h)")
MSG(67, COLORS,       R,  Any,   Session,   Colors,      Both,   session,   "u8 kind: the player colour table, a guest's choice")
MSG(68, REPORT,       R,  Any,   Session,   Report,      Both,   session,   "the session report (net/sreport.h)")
MSG(69, HOST_WORLD,   R,  Host,  Session,   HostWorld,   Both,   session,   "u32 world: the host's save changed (BUG-0933)")
MSG(70, HOST_BUSY,    R,  Host,  Session,   HostBusy,    Client, session,   "the host's game is paused, in an editor or away (busy_model.h, 14 bytes v1: u8 version, u8 state, u16 why, u32 mode, u32 world, u16 seq; BUG-1142)")
MSG(71, TRIBE_ANIM,   RU, Host,  Module,    Tribe,       Client, tribe,     "u8 kind (wire/tribe_anim.h), payload: the tribe members' animations, holds, air height, the theme and party music, the game-over and pause waits (MSG_NPC_ANIM's kinds 2-16, 20, 21 for a peer before tribe 1.1, BUG-1160)")
MSG(72, CELL_MATE,    RU, Guest, HostWorld, Cell,        Host,   cell,      "u8 kind: 0 (unreliable, 5 Hz) the pose of the mate its mating call brought: u32 res instance, u32 key[3], u8 level, f32 size, vec3 pos, f32 vx, vy, quat, f32 world scale; 1 (reliable) it is gone (BUG-1246)")
MSG(73, SPECIES_LINE, R,  Any,   Session,   SpeciesLine, Both,   creations, "u8 kind (species_line_core.h): a player's species line row, its stored row, a piece of a line creation (the host relays it; WP-0, BUG-1270)")
MSG(74, CIV_WALLET,   R,  Any,   HostWorld, CivWallet,   Both,   civ,       "every player's own Civ money (civ_wallet.h, civ.own_money, BUG-1468): u8 kind; guest -> host 1 an ask, 4 a report (u32 last seq applied, f64 money); host -> guest 2 the wallet, 3 a change (u32 seq, f64); only between peers of civ 1.2")
MSG(75, PLAYER_HISTORY, R, Any,  Session,   History,     Both,   session,   "u8 kind (wire/history.h): 1 host -> guest its own stage history (cards, trait progress), 2 guest -> host its own game's Cell card (WP-H1, BUG-1470)")
MSG(76, PROGRESS,     R,  Any,   HostWorld, Progress,    Both,   creature,  "own progress (all.shared_dna 2, own_progress_logic.h): u8 kind: guest ask / report of its own values, host values back / the players' table / a gain its game paid for the guest's deed (WP-P1/P2 of 0.7.17, BUG-1469)")
MSG(77, RESCUE,       R,  Any,   HostWorld, Rescue,      Both,   creature,  "a downed creature and its revive (revive_logic.h, creature.revive, WP-R1 of 0.7.17, BUG-1472): u8 kind, u32 world; guest -> host K_DOWN / K_GIVE_UP u32 knockout; host -> guest K_RESULT u32 knockout, u8 result, u8 price kind, f32 price; host -> guests K_LINES u8 n, n x {u8 player, u16 tenths left, u8 revive %}; only between peers of creature 1.3")
MSG(78, UFO_LEAD,     RU, Any,   Module,    Squadron,    Both,   space,     "u8 kind (wire/space_ufo.h): 0 a guest leader's ship state, 1 a follower's hit, 2 the leader's NPC hit on a follower, 3 the host's table of guest leaders per place; the NPC ships of a star system or planet without the host (the host relays; BUG-1288)")
MSG(79, ADVENTURE,    RU, Any,   Module,    Adventure,   Both,   creature,  "u8 kind (wire/adventure.h): co-op Galactic Adventures shared run journal (hello, welcome, goal propose/commit, act change, outcome, object deaths) and host-authoritative adventure creatures (actor batches, guest hit forwarding; WP-A, BUG-1474, BUG-0793)")
MSG(80, RIVALS,       R,  Any,   Session,   Rivals,      Both,   session,   "u8 kind (wire/rivals.h): Rivals shared systems (stage modes, 4x4 relations + 60 s war notice, influence, race progress & catch-up timer, draft, chronicle; WP-R1, BUG-0794)")
MSG(81, RIVALS_FACTION, R, Any,  Module,    RivalsFaction, Both, npc,       "u8 stage, u8 subkind (wire/rivals_faction.h): per-stage Rivals faction ownership, base sites, per-player NPC relations, alliance gifts, PvP, Space emigration (WP-R2..R6, BUG-1546..1550)")

#undef MSG
#undef FAMILY
